## Why This Is Asked

This question tests understanding of order statistics in dynamic sets, along with practical implementation details like lazy deletion and handling duplicates.

## Key Concepts

- **Median of a dynamic set**: the middle element (or average of two middle elements) when sorted
- **Two-heap approach**: max-heap for the lower half, min-heap for the upper half
- **Lazy deletion**: defer actual removal until top operations, tracking deletions via a count map
- **Duplicate handling**: maintain frequency counts rather than storing duplicate values multiple times in the heaps

## Code Example

```javascript
class MedianFinder {
  constructor() {
    this.low = new MaxHeap();    // max-heap for lower half
    this.high = new MinHeap();   // min-heap for upper half
    this.delayed = new Map();    // lazy deletion map
  }

  insert(num) {
    if (this.low.isEmpty() || num <= this.low.peek()) {
      this.low.push(num);
    } else {
      this.high.push(num);
    }
    this.rebalance();
  }

  rebalance() {
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size() + 1) {
      this.high.push(this.low.pop());
    } else if (this.high.size() > this.low.size()) {
      this.low.push(this.high.pop());
    }
  }

  erase(num) {
    this.delayed.set(num, (this.delayed.get(num) || 0) + 1);
    if (num <= this.low.peek()) {
      this.low.deleted++;
    } else {
      this.high.deleted++;
    }
    this.rebalance();
  }

  getMedian() {
    this.prune(this.low);
    this.prune(this.high);
    if (this.low.size() > this.high.size()) {
      return this.low.peek();
    }
    return (this.low.peek() + this.high.peek()) / 2;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests augmented BST design for duplicates and range queries on a dynamic multiset, focusing on balance, memory, and correctness.

## Key Concepts
- Treap with duplicates via per-node cnt
- Subtree size and sum augmentation
- kth smallest by counts; range queries via splits or traversal

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node{constructor(key,prio){this.key=key;this.prio=prio;this.cnt=1;this.l=null;this.r=null;this.sz=1;this.sum=key}};
function upd(n){if(!n)return; n.sz=n.cnt+(n.l?.sz||0)+(n.r?.sz||0); n.sum=n.key*n.cnt+(n.l?.sum||0)+(n.r?.sum||0)}
function rotateRight(y){const x=y.l; y.l=x.r; x.r=y; upd(y); upd(x); return x}
function rotateLeft(x){const y=x.r; x.r=y.l; y.l=x; upd(x); upd(y); return y}
function insert(n, key){if(!n)return new Node(key,Math.random()); if(key===n.key){n.cnt++; upd(n);return n}; if(key<n.key){n.l=insert(n.l,key); if(n.l.prio>n.prio) n=rotateRight(n);} else {n.r=insert(n.r,key); if(n.r.prio>n.prio) n=rotateLeft(n);} upd(n); return n}
function kth(n,k){if(!n) return null; const leftSize=n.l?.sz||0; if(k<=leftSize) return kth(n.l,k); if(k>leftSize+n.cnt) return kth(n.r,k-leftSize-n.cnt); return n.key;}
```

